WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.088
Booting is the sequence that prepares hardware and loads an operating system.

00:00:04.088 --> 00:00:07.154
Firmware begins before the operating system exists in RAM.

00:00:07.154 --> 00:00:12.265
It identifies a boot target, and a boot loader arranges for a kernel to run.

00:00:12.265 --> 00:00:14.990
Exact details vary across devices and firmware designs.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:16.422
No.

00:00:16.422 --> 00:00:21.601
Showing firmware output proves at least part of the display path works.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:27.212
The next investigation concerns boot-device detection, boot order, boot-loader configuration or OS startup.

00:00:27.212 --> 00:00:30.665
A failed login is a different, later-stage problem.

00:00:31.665 --> 00:00:33.576
Which normally starts first?

00:00:33.576 --> 00:00:36.920
Firmware executes before loading the operating system.
